{
  "case_id": "2020-20-222",
  "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plaintiffs allege that Goldman maintained an artificially inflated stock price by repeatedly making false and misleading generic statements about its ability to manage conficts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even so, that allocated burden will be outcome determinative only in the rare case in which the evidence is in perfect equipoise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sopan Joshi argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae in support of neither party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldman",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goldman argues that the Second Circuit erred twice: frst, by holding that the generic nature of its alleged misrepresentations is irrelevant to the price impact inquiry; and second, by assigning Goldman the burden of persuasion to prove a lack of price impact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0000-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goldman sought to defeat class certification by rebutting the Basic presumption through evidence that its alleged misrepresentations actually had no impact on its stock price."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The generic nature of a misrepresentation often will be important evidence of a lack of price impact, particularly in cases proceeding under the infation-maintenance theory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldman",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goldman also argues that the Second Circuit erred by requiring Goldman, rather than Plaintiffs, to bear the burden of persuasion on price impact at class certifcation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldman",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goldman relies exclusively on Federal Rule of Evidence 301, which provides in full: \u201cIn a civil case, unless a federal statute or these rules provide otherwise, the party against whom a presumption is directed has the burden of producing evidence to rebut the presumption. But this rule does not shift the burden of persuasion, which remains on the party who had it originally.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thus, the best reading of our precedents\u2014as the Courts of Appeals to have considered the issue have recognized\u2014is that the defendant bears the burden of persuasion to prove a lack of price impact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldman",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General statements, like those challenged here, are incapable of impacting a company's stock price as a matter of law\u201d because they are \u201c `too general to cause a reasonable investor to rely upon them.' \u201d Brief for Appellants in No. 18\u20133667 (CA2), pp. 43, 46."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "From start to fnish, the plaintiff has the\nburden to satisfy that essential element of its claim. Basic's\npresumption of reliance thus \u201cdoes not shift\u201d any burden of\npersuasion\u2014that always \u201cremains\u201d with the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Upon such a showing, the presumption of reliance drops from\nthe case and the trier of fact must decide the question of\nreliance vel non, cognizant of the fact the plaintiff bears the\nburden of proving reliance like any other essential elements\nof its claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court disputes none of this. It does not even try to\ndefend on the merits its unusual suggestion that the defend-\nant carries some burden of persuasion in a plaintiff's claim\nfor securities fraud."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f63bb538fd6b0a9af67d4588b3d65fef090ae457a7503196b09e822b7e304129",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f63bb538fd6b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respectfully, I dissent."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
